# Kanban bug cards

When a feature file has frontmatter `labels: ["bug"]`, follow [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Bug cards.

## Frontmatter (agent creates)

```yaml
labels: ["bug"]
```

Use the **inline JSON array** form exactly — not a YAML block list (`labels:\n  - bug`).

## User provides

- `## Steps to Reproduce`
- `## Current Behavior` (legacy: `## What happens`)
- `## Expected Behavior`
- `## Feature Areas`
- `## QA Review` (during Review, if follow-up issues found)

## Agent provides (pre-implementation card review, before `in-progress`)

- `## Root Cause (current code)` — after reading Product scope + codebase
- `## Acceptance Criteria` — behavior-only fix bullets
- `## Out of Scope` — optional
- `## Product Paths` — resolved from Feature Areas via `docs/feature-areas.yaml` (no `tests/`)
- `## Product Methods` — symbols to edit (when Feature Areas set)
- `## Tests` — **Files**, **Methods**, **Verify (agent)**
- `## Docs` — doc paths + § hints
- `## Corrective Action` — concrete fix plan (**not** `## Decisions`); append **`**QA follow-up (YYYY-MM-DD):**`** bullets when fixing Review issues (§ User-reported QA fixes)

**Legacy alias:** `done/` / `archived/` cards may use **Label Paths** / **Label Methods** — parsers read
as Product (Signature: `kanban-card-scope-schema`).

## User-reported QA fixes

When fixing **Review** issues the user reports (chat, screenshots, or **`## QA Review`**):

1. Implement the fix; run targeted pytest when code changes.
2. **Append** a dated `**QA follow-up (YYYY-MM-DD):**` bullet under **`## Corrective Action`** — symptom, fix, test/doc pointer; add **`Scope:`** note when Product/Tests/Docs were appended.
3. **Refresh scope on the card** (same turn, when code changed):
   - **`## Feature Areas`** — append area label if fix crossed into a new product area.
   - **`## Product Paths`** — append any edited/added product paths not already listed.
   - **`## Product Methods`** — append symbols touched.
   - **`## Tests`** — append test files / `test_*` methods.
   - **`## Docs`** — append doc paths when user-visible docs changed.
   - **`docs/feature-areas.yaml`** — when new paths/handlers are durable for that area.
4. Bump `modified`. Optionally mark matching **`## QA Review`** `[x]`.

**Do not** skip the card update — the card is the audit trail. Full workflow: kanban-markdown § User-reported QA fixes.

## Card Done — lessons learned

When the user signals **QA-complete / Done** on a bug card, the **agent** moves to `done/` and runs
Card Done **same turn** (Signature: `card-done-agent-move-qa-complete`). Checklist:
[kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Card Done — lessons learned capture.

## Do not

- Use `## Decisions` on bug cards — use `## Corrective Action`
- Start implementation with empty or disputed **Corrective Action**
- Move to **Review** without all **Acceptance Criteria** marked `[x]`
- Put method names only in **Product Paths** — use **Product Methods** (files-only paths in Product Paths; tests in **Tests**)
- Treat **deferred scope** on a parent feature card (documented Out of Scope) as a bug — spawn a **feature** card instead unless behavior contradicts shipped AC
- **Properties inspector / Save Layer** — variant, material, or direction changes with a selected cell but no dirty flag → `brush_inspector_changed` + `_apply_inspector_to_selected_cell`; Signature: `properties-inspector-live-apply` ([ui-change/SKILL.md](../skills/ui-change/SKILL.md) § Properties brush — live apply)

## Spawn from parent QA Review

Parent **`## QA Review`** + **`## Spawned bug cards`** table; child `labels: ["bug"]`, `status: todo`,
same `epic` when phased. Product-specific spawn hints (orbit, Floating Camera, properties inspector):
[testing.mdc](testing.mdc) + area skills — grep **Signature** before spawning.

